# AILit Framework

#### AI Literacy Frameworks are being developed to support educators in brining AI relevant skills into the classroom.


#### The **AILit Framework** is a joint initiative of the European Commission and the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD). Code.org and leading international experts support its development.


#### The AILit Framework provides a starting point for helping students understand and use AI in thoughtful, responsible ways. It is designed for all educators and can be integrated into existing subjects and lessons.

#### The framework is organized around three key elements that work together:

<div style="max-width:1000px; margin:20px auto; font-family:ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial;">

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap:20px;">

<!-- KNOWLEDGE -->
<div style="border:1px solid #5a2ca0; border-radius:18px; padding:20px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; margin-bottom:12px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/01bcfdad34fbe94df49a42fa383600d1-Screenshot 2026-03-30 at 10.59.49 AM.png" style="width:40px;">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:20px;">Knowledge</div>
</div>
<div style="margin-bottom:10px;">
Knowledge focuses on what students understand about AI.
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px;">
<strong>Example:</strong> AI reflects human choices and can include bias from the data it is trained on.
</div>
</div>

<!-- SKILLS -->
<div style="border:1px solid #5a2ca0; border-radius:18px; padding:20px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; margin-bottom:12px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/80cec506af206a17886dd8e93fddc5ce-Screenshot 2026-03-30 at 10.59.44 AM.png" style="width:40px;">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:20px;">Skills</div>
</div>
<div style="margin-bottom:10px;">
Skills focus on what students can do when working with AI.
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px;">
<strong>Example:</strong> Creativity: using AI to generate and refine ideas while staying responsible for the final product.
</div>
</div>

<!-- ATTITUDES -->
<div style="border:1px solid #5a2ca0; border-radius:18px; padding:20px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; margin-bottom:12px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/a15746db2cd10f74f27ff30a58119a8b-Screenshot 2026-03-30 at 10.59.39 AM.png" style="width:40px;">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:20px;">Attitudes</div>
</div>
<div style="margin-bottom:10px;">
Attitudes focus on how students approach AI.
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px;">
<strong>Example:</strong> Responsible: thinking carefully about how AI is used and its potential impact.
</div>
</div>

</div>
</div>


#### Rather than focusing only on technical concepts, the framework emphasizes helping students think critically, make informed decisions, and use AI in ways that support learning and human judgment.

#### The framework is flexible and meant to be applied across grade levels and subjects. Teachers can use it to identify small, meaningful ways to incorporate AI-related thinking into the lessons they already teach.

